  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming wildlife conservation and livelihoods at the landscape scale in Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mozambique&#x2019;s globally significant biodiversity is under increasing threat from illegal wildlife trade, habitat loss, and unsustainable land-use practices, compounded by poverty, population pressure, and weak governance. The Gorongosa&#x2013;Marromeu and Rovuma&#x2013;Lugenda landscapes are priority ecosystems facing rising deforestation, poaching, and human-wildlife conflict.The objective of the project is to strengthen the integrated management of wildlife conservation and the improvement of livelihoods in t</narrative>
  </description>
